A||N||1||FIERO1985||Timing Chain On a V6||||1||
Z||000000||FIERO1985||03-24-2001||04:42 PM||||Ok, it is now time to put a timing chain on my 85 gt, is there any advice on how to make the job smoother I wish I replaced it last month when I did the water pump and the balancer at the same time!!! But What are the steps and what is the best way to go about it. And also what do I need to buy (parts and accessories...) I already did the pump and balancer! ThaNKS aLOT FOR HELP<P><BR>DAN<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000001||2birds||03-24-2001||10:42 PM||||Make sure you follow the torque specs in your Haynes or Chilton manual.<BR>Don't forget to have the permatex sealant, a new balancer seal, and a sleeve kit if it already has a groove worn into the balancer.  I like rubbing alcohol for stubborn gaskets, and a scraper.  You'll need a gear puller for the lower gear, and I'd change the oil and filter in case you get any crap in the pan, and more anti-freeze.  Lots of brake cleaner to clean parts with, too.<BR>An inspection mirror is handy, and a soft hammer to knock the timing cover loose after you are POSITIVE you have ALL the bolts out.  <P>The extra elbow and wrist you had put in for the water pump job will come in handy again, too.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Don't forget patience.<BR>||||reg||1
